# Igris USER — your local override surface

This file lives at `~/.igris/USER.md`. It's preserved across `igris init --upgrade`
operations byte-for-byte. Use it for personal notes that should NOT live in any
project repo (because the brain is per-user, not per-project).

## User identity

- name: {{USER_NAME}}
- email: {{USER_EMAIL}}

## Notes

This file is YOURS. `igris init --upgrade` preserves it byte-for-byte and never
clobbers your notes. The identity fields and the `## Preferences` block are
managed for you — `igris init`, `igris configure`, and `/setup` write them when
you update your settings; edit any other content freely and it is preserved.

Some fields drive runtime behavior, not just display: e.g. your addressing
preference feeds the persona greeting at boot. Change these via `igris configure`
or `/setup` (each edit is shown and confirmed) rather than by hand when you can.
